A **non-deterministic finite state automaton** M = (Q, δ, Q0, F) with input alphabet X consists of:

- a **finite set Q of states**;
- a **transition relation δ : Q × (X ∪ {λ}) → 2^Q**, associating with (q, x) a possibly empty set of states δ(q, x) ⊆ Q, where 2^Q is the set of all subsets of Q;
- a **possibly empty set Q0 ⊆ Q of start states**;
- a **set F ⊆ Q of accepting states**.

When in state q reading x ∈ X the machine may move to any state in δ(q, x), and may also move to any state in δ(q, λ) without using up any input.

**Acceptance:** a string is accepted if **one** of the paths it defines ends in an accepting state; otherwise it is not accepted. All the letters must be used — no premature termination.
